  "verbalization": "Goiazensolide is shown to have a target relationship with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through multiple pathways. The first pathway links Goiazensolide to amine oxidase, a flavin-containing enzyme, which in turn is targeted by a complex compound. This complex then targets CDC2L1, suggesting a potential regulatory role in the kinase pathway. The second pathway connects Goiazensolide to protein kinase C eta, which is targeted by monamine, and ultimately also targets CDC2L1. The third pathway similarly links Goiazensolide to protein kinase C eta, which is targeted by K-strophanthin-beta, which also targets CDC2L1. These findings collectively suggest that Goiazensolide may modulate the activity of CDC2L1 through different downstream targets, potentially influencing cellular processes involving kinase activity. The evidence supports a broader role for Goiazensolide in interacting with the CDC2L1 pathway, though the exact mechanism and extent of its influence remain to be fully elucidated."
